        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/432915?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This adds a new guide in \"Defenses\" on \"operational security\", which I've defined basically as processes around developing, building, shipping, and updating software.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It overlaps considerably with supply chain security, and most of its content is taken from the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Security/Attacks/Supply_chain_attacks\" rel=\"nofollow\">Supply chain attacks</a> article. It's not a complete overlap though, in particular we talk about logging and monitoring in this guide, and we talk about SRI in supply chain security but not in this guide.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44065",
