        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/137640490?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Re-parsing and mutated XSS (mXSS) security section explaining innerHTML round-trip risk, example unsafe flow, mitigation recommendations along with reference</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n Make readers to avoid risk and stay updated\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n <span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #43386.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4046479684\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43386\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43386/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43386\">#43386</a>\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43990",
            "title": "Element.setHTML(): add mXSS warning about re-parsing sanitized HTML",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-04T03:38:38.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-03T10:58:40.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "narasimhan-lakshmi",
                "url": "https://github.com/narasimhan-lakshmi"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13959985?u=c9ed763913289f3328a467148f1c4bbe09e93e7a&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Explain that the example uses theProtoObj and handler without declaring them, which may lead to a ReferenceError when copied directly. Add explicit variable declarations to make the example self-contained and runnable.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The current example may confuse readers, especially beginners, because it assumes the existence of variables that are not defined in the snippet. Making the example self-contained improves clarity and ensures it works when copied and tested directly.</p>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43979",
            "title": "Fix missing variable declarations in object example",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-02T03:26:06.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-01T03:43:44.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "mostafahamed15",
                "url": "https://github.com/mostafahamed15"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 144 adds support for the <code class=\"notranslate\">visibilitymaskchange</code> event/<code class=\"notranslate\">XRVisibilityMaskChange</code> event object; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5073760055066624\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5073760055066624</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds documentation for:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>The <code class=\"notranslate\">XRVisibilityMaskChange</code> event object and all its members.</li>\n<li>The <code class=\"notranslate\">visibilitymaskchange</code> event</li>\n<li>The <code class=\"notranslate\">XRView.index</code> property.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
